From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ludovic Henry <git@ludovic.dev>
Date: Fri, 11 Sep 2026 19:40:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] MANIFEST.in: include tests/ in the sdist

Upstream's own pyproject.toml cibuildwheel config
(`before-test = "pip install -r {project}/tests/requirements.txt"`,
`test-command = "pytest {project}/tests"`) assumes the tests/ tree is present
next to the built package. That's true when cibuildwheel runs directly
against a git checkout, but MANIFEST.in never adds tests/ to the sdist, so
building wheels from the sdist (as this port does, to build the
architecture-independent sdist once instead of once per riscv64 matrix leg)
fails before-test with "No such file or directory: tests/requirements.txt".
Once that's fixed, test_lib.py's success-rate tests still need the
extensionless calibration data files under tests/calibration/ (read via
success_count_functions/load_success_count_calibration), so the include
covers all of tests/, not just its .py/.txt files. Confirmed the published
PyPI sdist for 0.2.22 has the same gap.

Upstream-Status: To upstream [not yet submitted; needs a minorminer maintainer decision on whether tests/ belongs in the sdist or their own CI should build from a checkout instead]
---
 MANIFEST.in | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

diff --git a/MANIFEST.in b/MANIFEST.in
index 5ca6dec..d8244e0 100644
--- a/MANIFEST.in
+++ b/MANIFEST.in
@@ -4,3 +4,4 @@ recursive-include external/glasgow-subgraph-solver *.hh LICENSE
 recursive-include external/portable-snippets builtin.h COPYING.md
 recursive-include external barrier
 recursive-include minorminer/_extern LICENSE.md
+recursive-include tests *
